	(text "Wheel counters\n\nThey are placed near the wheel, soldered upside down on the back layer"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 82.55 105.41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0dec372e-0d1d-44f2-a147-58016ecb5f67")
	)
	(text "Audio\n\n- I2S Class D amplifier, driving a speaker (4ohm, 3W)\nat the front.\n- I2S Digital Microphone, at the back far from\nthe front speaker. This module \nhas pre-filtering capabilies, high sampling\nrate and hight resolution (16bits) suitable\nfor sound re-cognition.\n- 2 x Analog microphones, they are also fit for\nDSP application by tuning the gain. The intend\nhowever is to detect just sound and its \nenergy in attempt to locate the source. \nWith 3 mics positioned back, lef and right, \nthis should help triangulate.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 93.98 219.71 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "435bf7fa-cfab-4243-9954-7806d72ea2c4")
	)
	(text "Analog mics on right and left sides"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 118.11 198.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5e03ab16-1a21-4145-941a-d801ada33ccb")
	)
	(text "POWER\nBattery 21700 (3.7V) for maximum power density.\nThegulator to provide 5V with cutoff on low voltage to \nprotect the battery. The resistors to EN are computed \nso that to cutoff at 3.0V (when EN = 1V), and low enough \nso that the EN current is negligeable. The tolerance for \nthese resistors should be at most 0.1% for precise \ncutoff at 3V.  The max load at 3.7V input is ~2.5 A."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 68.58 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "60836d30-130f-4900-866e-0bc88e55a57e")
	)
	(text "Level shifting from 3.3V to 5V, from ESP32 S3 CAM A for the leds, and I2C signals"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6c4c3cc8-cc8d-4bbf-9f47-b277109f90b0")
	)
